 ### [GGX Mixture NDF](10859-ggx-mixture-ndf.md)
-The GGX Mixture NDF is a compact representation of the marginal distribution of surface normals, $p_N(n)$, used to model the glossiness and anisotropy of aggregated microflake appearances. It solves the problem of representing complex, arbitrarily oriented surface normal distributions by combining multiple SGGX lobes. It is distinguished from single-lobe SGGX by its ability to capture multi-modal or highly anisotropic normal distributions through a weighted sum, building on the [SGGX Microflake Distribution](6660-sggx-microflake-distribution.md).
+The GGX Mixture NDF is a compact representation of the marginal distribution of surface normals, $p_N(n)$, used to model the glossiness and anisotropy of aggregated microflake appearances. It solves the problem of representing complex, arbitrarily oriented surface normal distributions by combining multiple SGGX lobes. It is distinguished from single-lobe SGGX by its ability to capture multi-modal or highly anisotropic normal distributions through a weighted sum, building on the [SGGX Microflake Distribution](6660-sggx-microflake-distribution.md). Choose it when the target microflake ensemble exhibits multi-modal or highly anisotropic normal distributions that a single lobe cannot capture.
 
